menu "espix fault handling"

    config ESPIX_FAULT_REAP
        bool "Reap the faulting task instead of rebooting (NOT IMPLEMENTED)"
        default n
        help
            Placeholder for the "a crashing app does not crash the system"
            path: instead of delegating to ESP-IDF's panic handler (dump and
            reboot), hand the faulting task to the espix reaper and resume.

            This does nothing yet, and turning it on will not change behaviour.
            Before it can, three things need solving — locks held by the dead
            task, per-process ownership of heap/fds so reaping does not leak,
            and deciding which fault classes are recoverable at all. See the
            comments at the top of reaper.c.

endmenu
